  "init": [
    {
      "_comment": "Task 12 fix round 2 (spec 2026-08-12-modulation-pace S3.3), the Sampler half of the pair split from flow_pace_sweep.json -- see that file's init comment for the full account of why a scenario-side set_engine override is unsafe (it silently disables the BBD RANGE cap, flow.cpp:576-580) and why one terrain can never draw BOTH Sampler and BBD (taste.h:659-666: carrier is structurally restricted to {SYNTH, WAVE, BODY}, so one deck is always a carrier and never Sampler/BBD -- the 'loud pair' exclusion is by construction, not chance). F1-00000011-000000000000 is a terrain whose own draw (roles_of(), checked directly with a scratch probe over master seeds 0..200000) naturally assigns ENGINE_SAMPLER to deck A and ENGINE_SYNTH (the carrier) to deck B, with no scenario override needed -- so this file also doubles as a synth-envelope render, the same way flow_pace_sweep.json's BBD deck pairs with a natural SYNTH carrier on its own deck B.",
      "action": "flow_wake",
      "value": "F1-00000011-000000000000"
    },
    {
      "action": "flow_macro",
      "slot": 0,
      "value": 0.5
    },
    {
      "action": "flow_macro",
      "slot": 1,
      "value": 0.5
    },
    {
      "action": "flow_macro",
      "slot": 2,
      "value": 0.5
